hadiths[328]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3370","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: “There is nothing more honorable with Allah [Most High] than supplication.”"
"3371","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Prophet said: “The supplication is the essence of worship.”"
"3372","An-Nu`man bin Bashir narrated that:The Prophet said: “The supplication"
"3373","Abu Hurairah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Indeed"
"3374","Abu Musa Al-Ash`ari (ra) said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a military expedition. When we returned"
"3375","Abdullah bin Busr (ra) narrated that:A man said: “O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3376","Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri narrated that:The Messenger of Allah was asked: “Which of the worshippers is superior in rank with Allah on the Day of Judgment?” He said: “Those men who remember Allah much [and women].” He said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! What about the fighter in the cause of Allah?’ He said: ‘If he were to strike with his sword among the disbelievers and the idolater"
"3377","Abu Ad-Darda [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that :the Prophet said: “Should I not inform you of the best of your deed"
"3378","Al-Agharr Abu Muslim narrated that:He bears witness"
"3379","Abu Sa’eed Al Khudri narrated the:Mu’awiyah came out to the Masjid and said: “What has caused you to gather for this sitting.” They said: “We gathered so that we may remember Allah.” He said"
"3380","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that :the Prophet said: “No group gather in a sitting in which they do not remember Allah"
"3381","Jabir narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: “There is none who utters a supplication"
"3382","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever wishes that Allah would respond to him during hardship and grief"
"3383","Jabir bin `Abdullah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best remembrance is: ‘there is none worthy of worship except Allah (Lā ilāha illallāh)’ and the best supplication is: ‘All praise is due to Allah (Al-ḥamdulillāh).’”"
"3384","A'ishah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to remember Allah in all of his affairs"
"3385","Ibn `Abbas narrated from Ubayy bin Ka`b that :whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would mention someone and supplicate for him"
"3386","Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated:“Whenever the Messenger of Allah would raise his hands in supplication"
"3387","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: “One of you will be responded to"
"3388","Aban bin `Uthman said:“I heard `Uthman bin `Affan (ra) saying: ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no worshiper who says"
"3389","Thawban (ra) said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘Whoever says when he reaches the evening: “I am pleased with Allah as (my) Lord"
"3390","Abdullah said:“When he reached the evening"
"3391","Abu Hurairah (ra) said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to teach his Companions"
"3392","Abu Hurairah"
"3393","Shaddad bin Aws narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: “Should I not direct you to the chief of supplications for forgiveness? ‘O Allah"
"3394","Al-Bara' bin `Azib narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: “Should I not teach you some words to say when you go to your bed"
"3395","Rafi` bin Khadij narrated that:The Prophet said: “When one of you lies down on his right side"
"3396","Anas bin Malik (ra) narrated that :when he went to his bed"
"3397","Abu Sa`eed (ra) narrated that :the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says"
"3398","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman (ra) narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) would sleep"
"3399","Al-Bara' bin `Azib (ra) narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to lay his head upon his right hand when going to sleep"
"3400","Abu Hurairah (ra) said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to order that when one of us went to sleep"
"3401","Abu Hurairah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When one of you leaves his bed then returns to it"
"3402","Aishah narrated that:Every night"
"3403","Farwah bin Nawfal (ra) narrated that:He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: “O Messenger of Allah"
"3404","Jabir said:“The Prophet would not sleep until he reached Tanzil as-Sajdah and Tabarak.”"
"3405","A'isha (ra) said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) would not sleep until he recited Az-Zumar and Banu Isra’il.” Muhammad bin Ismail informed me: “This Abu Lubabah’s (a narrator in the chain) name is Marwan"
"3406","Ar-Irbad bin Sariyah (ra) narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) would not sleep until he had recited Al-Musabbihat"
"3407","A man from Banu Hanzalah said:“I accompanied Shaddad bin Aws [may Allah be pleased with him] on a journey"
"3408","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“Fatimah complained to me about her hands blistering from grinding flour. So I said: ‘If you were to approach your father and ask him for a servant?’ So he (the Prophet) said: ‘Should I not direct the two of you"
"3409","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“Fatimah went to the Prophet complaining of her hands blistering"
"3410","Abdullah bin `Amr [may Allah be pleased with both of them] said:“The Messenger of Allah said: ‘There are two characteristics over which a Muslim man does not guard"
"3411","Abdullah bin Amr [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“I saw the Messenger of Allah counting At-Tasbīḥ.”"
"3412","Ka’b bin Ujrah narrated that:The Prophet said: “There are Mu’aqqibat"
"3413","Zaid bin Thabit (ra) said:“We were ordered to say the Tasbīḥ at the end of every Salat thirty-three times"
"3414","Ubadah bin As-Samit"
"3415","Maslamah bin `Amr said:“`Umair bin Hani used to perform a thousand prostrations every day and recite a hundred thousand Tasbīḥs every day.”"
"3416","Rabi`ah bin Ka`b Al-Aslami said:“I used to spend the night at the door of the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3417","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that when the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to sleep"
"3418","Abdullah bin `Abbas [may Allah be pleased with them] narrated"
"3419","Ibn Abbas said:“One night"
"3420","Abu Salamah said:“I asked Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]: ‘With what did the Prophet used to open his Salat when he stood up in the night?’ She said: ‘When he stood up in the night"
"3421","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that whenever the Messenger of Allah would stand for Salat"
"3422","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that whenever the Messenger of Allah would stand for Salat"
"3423","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that :when the Messenger of Allah would stand for the obligatory prayer"
"3424","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid said:“Ibn Juraij said to me: “Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid informed me that Ibn Abbas said: “A man came to the Prophet and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! I had a dream at night while I was sleeping"
"3425","Aishah narrated:“When the Messenger of Allah would prostrate (for recitation of) the Qur’an"
"3426","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says – that is: when he leaves his house – ‘In the Name of Allah"
"3427","Umm Salamah narrated that :When the Prophet (ﷺ) would leave his house"
"3428","Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar narrated from his father"
"3429","Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar narrates from his father"
"3430","Al-Agharr Abu Muslim narrated that he bears witness from Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah"
"3431","Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sees a person afflicted and say: ‘All praise is due to Allah Who saved me from that which He has afflicted you with"
"3432","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sees an afflicted person then says: ‘All praise is due to Allah who saved me from that which He has afflicted you with"
"3433","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sits in a sitting and engages in much empty"
"3434","Ibn Umar said:“In one sitting of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3435","Ibn Abbas narrated that :when he was in distress"
"3436","Abu Hurairah narrated that:When a matter would worry the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3437","Sa`d bin Abi Waqqas narrated:From Khawlah bint Al Hakim As-Sulamiyyah"
"3438","Abu Hurairah narrated:“When the Prophet (ﷺ) would travel"
"3439","Abdullah bin Sarjis narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to travel"
"3440","Ar-Rabi` bin Al-Bara’ bin `Azib reported from"
"3441","Anas narrated that:When the Prophet would return from a trip and see the walls of Al-Madinah"
"3442","Ibn Umar narrated"
"3443","Salim narrated that :when he intended to undertake a journey"
"3444","Anas said:“A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ‘I intend to undertake a journey"
"3445","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that :a man said: “O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3446","Ali bin Rabi’ah said:“I witnessed Ali having an animal brought to him to ride. When he placed his foot in the stirrup he said: ‘In the Name of Allah"
"3447","Ibn `Umar narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to travel"
"3448","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated :that the Messenger of Allah said: “Three supplications are responded to: The supplication of the oppressed"
"3449","Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her] narrates"
"3450","Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar narrated :from his father"
"3451","Bilal bin Yahya bin Talhah bin `Ubaidullah narrated :from his father"
"3452","Mu`adh bin Jabal narrated :that one of the two men cursed the other next to the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3453","Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri narrated that:He heard the Prophet saying: “When one of you sees a dream that he likes"
"3454","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrates"
"3455","Ibn Abbas narrated:“I entered with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3456","Abu Umamah narrated that :when the table spread would be lifted from in front of him"
"3457","Abu Sa`eed [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) used to eat or drink"
"3458","Sahl bin Mu`adh bin Anas narrated from his father that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever eats food and then says: ‘All praise is due to Allah who fed me this and granted it as provision to me"
"3459","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that:The Prophet said: “when you hear the crowing of the roosters"
"3460","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “there is not anyone upon the earth who says: ‘None has the right to be worshipped but Allah"
"3461","Abu Musa Al-Ash`ari said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a military expedition. When we returned"
"3462","Ibn Mas`ud narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I met Ibrahim on the night of my ascent"
"3463","Mus`ab bin Sa`d narrated from his father"
"3464","Jabir narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says: ‘Glory is to Allah"
"3465","Jabir narrated that :The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says: ‘Glory is to Allah"
"3466","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says: ‘Glory is to Allah"
"3467","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are two statements that are light on the tongue"
"3468","Abu Hurairah narrates that:The Mesenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says: ‘There is none worthy of worship except Allah"
"3469","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says in the morning and in the evening ‘Glory is to Allah and with His Praise (Subḥān Allāh"
"3470","Ibn `Umar narrated that one day"
"3471","Amr bin Shu`aib narrated from his father"
"3472","Az-Zuhri said:“A Tasbihah in Ramadan is better than a thousand Tasbihah in other that it.”"
"3473","Tamim Ad-Dari narrated that:The Messsenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says ten times: ‘I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah. Alone"
"3474","Abu Dharr narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says at the end of every Fajr prayer"
"3475","Abdullah bin Buraidah Al Aslami narrated from his father"
"3476","Fadalah bin `Ubaid narrated:“While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was seated"
"3477","Amr bin Malik Al-Janbi narrated that he heard Fadalah bin `Ubaid saying:“The Prophet (ﷺ) heard a man supplicating in his Salat but he did not send Salat upon the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3478","Asma bint Yazid narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Allah's greatest name is in these two Ayah: ‘And your deity is One deity"
"3479","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Call upon Allah while being certain of being answered"
"3480","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say:“O Allah"
"3481","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Fatimah came to the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3482","Abdullah bin `Amr narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: “O Allah"
"3483","Imran bin Husain narrated:“The Prophet (ﷺ) said to my father: ‘O Husain"
"3484","Anas bin Mallik [may Allah be pleased with him] narrates"
"3485","Anas narrated that :The Prophet (ﷺ) used to supplicate"
"3486","Abdullah bin Amr narrated:“I saw the Prophet counting the Tasbih on his hand.”"
"3487","Anas bin Malik narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) visited a man who was so emaciated that he had become like a baby bird. He (ﷺ) said to him: “And did you not used to supplicate? Did you not used to ask Your Lord for sound health?” He said: “I used to say: “O Allah"
"3488","Hisham bin Hassan narrated from Al-Hasan :concerning the saying of Allah: O our Lord"
"3489","Abdullah narrated that :the Prophet (ﷺ) used to supplicate: “O Allah"
"3490","Abu Ad-Darda’ narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It used to be from the supplication of Dawud that he would say: ‘O Allah"
"3491","Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khatmi Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say in his supplication:“O Allah grant me Your love and the love of those whose love will benefit me with You. O Allah"
"3492","Shakal bin Humaid said:""I came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"3493","Aishah narrated:“I was sleeping at the side of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3494","Abdullah bin `Abbas narrated:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used [to teach them this supplication as he used] to teach them a Surat of the Quran: “O Allah"
"3495","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to supplicate with these words:“O Allah"
"3496","Aishah said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying at his death: ‘O Allah"
"3497","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“None of you should say: ‘O Allah forgive me if You wish. O Allah have mercy on me if You wish.’ Let him be firm in asking"
"3498","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“Our Lord descends every night to the nearest heaven"
"3499","Abu Umamah narrated:“It was said: ‘O Messenger of Allah"
"3500","Abu Hurairah narrated that a man said:“O Messenger of Allah"
"3501","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says in the morning: ‘O Allah we have reached morning"
"3502","Ibn `Umar said:“Rarely would the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stand from a sitting until he supplicated with these words for his Companions: ‘O Allah"
"3503","Muslim bin Abi Bakrah said:“My father heard me while I was saying: “O Allah"
"3504","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: ‘Should I not teach you some words that if you say them"
"3505","Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Sa`d narrated from his father"
"3506","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated the the Prophet said:“Indeed Allah has ninety-nine Names"
"3507","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Indeed"
"3508","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet said:“Indeed"
"3509","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“When you pass by the gardens of Paradise"
"3510","Anas bin Malik [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“When you pass by the gardens of Paradise"
"3511","Umar bin Abu Salamah narrated from his mother"
"3512","Anas bin Malik narrated that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said:“O Messenger of Allah"
"3513","Aishah narrated:“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah"
"3514","Al-`Abbas bin `Abdul-Muttalib said:“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah"
"3515","Ibn Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said (ﷺ):“Allah has not been asked for anything more beloved to Him than being asked for Al-`Āfiyah"
"3516","Aishah narrated from Abu Bakr As-Siddiq"
"3517","Abu Malik Al-Ash`ari narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“Al-Wudu is half of faith"
"3518","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“At-Tasbīḥ is half of the Scale"
"3519","A man from Banu Sulaim narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) counted them out in my hand” - or - “in his hand: ‘At-Tasbīḥ is half of the Scale"
"3520","Ali bin Abi Talib said:“The most of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated with during the afternoon at Arafat while standing was: ‘O Allah to You is the praise like the one You say"
"3521","Abu Umamah narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated with many supplications of which we did not preserve a thing. We said: ‘O Messenger of Allah"
"3522","Shahr bin Hawshab said:“I said to Umm Salamah: ‘O Mother of the Believers! What was the supplication that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said most frequently when he was with you?” She said: ‘The supplication he said most frequently was: “O Changer of the hearts"
"3523","Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrated that his father said:“Khalid bin Al-Walid al Makhzumi complained to the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: ‘O Messenger of Allah"
"3524","Anas bin Malik said:“Whenever a matter would distress him"
"3525","Anas narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Be constant with: ‘O Possessor of Majesty and Honor (Yā Dhal-Jalāli wal-Ikrām).’”"
"3526","Abu Umamah Al-Bahili said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Whoever goes to his bed while in a state of purity and remembering Allah"
"3527","Mu`adh bin Jabal narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard a man supplicating"
"3528","Amr bin Shu`aib narrated from his father"
"3529","Abu Rashid Al-Hubrani said:“I came to `Abdullah bin `Amr and said to him: ‘Report something to me that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).’ So he set forth before me a scroll and said: ‘This is what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wrote for me.’” He said: “So I looked in it and found in it: ‘Indeed"
"3530","Amr bin Murrah said:“I heard Abu Wa’il say: ‘`Abdullah bin Mas`ud said’ and I said to him: ‘Did you hear it from `Abdullah?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ And he narrated it in Marfu` form that he said: ‘There is none with more Ghirah than Allah"
"3531","Abdullah bin `Amr narrated from Abu Bakr As-Siddiq that he said:“O Messenger of Allah"
"3532","Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada`ah said:“Al-`Abbas came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and it is as if he heard something"
"3533","Anas bin Malik narrated that:the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a tree with dry leaves"
"3534","Umarah bin Shabib As-Saba’i narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says: none has the right to be worshipped but Allah"
"3535","Zirr bin Hubaish said:“I came to Safwan bin `Assal Al Muradi to ask him about wiping over the Khuff"
"3536","Zirr bin Hubaish said:“I came to Safwan bin `Assal Al-Muradi so he said to me: ‘What has brought you"
"3537","Ibn `Umar narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Indeed Allah accepts the repentance of a slave as long as (his soul does not reach his throat).”"
"3538","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah is more delighted with the repentance of one of you"
"3539","Abu Sirmah narrated from Abu Ayyub"
"3540","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah"
"3541","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah created a hundred mercies"
"3542","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“If the believer knew what is with Allah of punishment"
"3543","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Verily"
"3544","Anas said that:The Prophet (ﷺ) entered the Masjid and there was a man who had performed Salat and was supplicating. He was saying in his supplication: “O Allah"
"3545","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“May the man before whom I am mentioned - and he does not send Salat upon me - be humiliated. And may a man upon whom Ramadan enters and then passes"
"3546","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The stingy person is the one before whom I am mentioned"
"3547","Abdullah bin [Abi] Awfa narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say:“O Allah"
"3548","Ibn `Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whomsoever of you the door of supplication is opened for"
"3549","That was narrated to us by Al-Qasim bin Dinar Al-Kufi (who said):“Ishaq bin Mansur narrated to us"
"3550","Abu Hurairah narrates"
"3551","Ibn `Abbas said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) used to supplicate"
"3552","Aishah narrated"
"3553","Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says ten times: ‘None has the right to be worshipped by Allah"
"3554","Saffiyah narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me and before me were four thousand date pits"
"3555","Ibn Abbas narrated from Juwairiyyah bint Al-Harith"
"3556","Salman Al-Farsi narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Indeed"
"3557","Abu Hurairah narrated that:A man was supplicating with his two fingers so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Make it one"
"3558","Mu`adh bin Rifa`ah narrated from his father"
"3559","Abu Bakr narrated:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who seeks forgiveness has not been persistent in sin"
"3560","Abu Umamah narrated:That `Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] wore a new garment and said: “All praise is due to Allah who clothed me with what I may cover my `Awrah"
"3561","Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated:That the Prophet (ﷺ) sent an expedition in the direction of Najd. They gained many spoils of war and returned quickly. A man among those who did not go out said: “We have not seen an expedition quicker in return or greater in spoils than this expedition.” So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Should I not direct you to a group greater in spoils and quicker in return? A group who attended Salat As-Subh"
"3562","Ibn `Umar narrated from `Umar:that he sought permission from the Prophet (ﷺ) concerning `Umrah"
"3563","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated:that a Mukatib came to him and said: “Indeed I am not capable of my Kitabah so aid me.” He said: “Should I not teach you words that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught me? If you had a debt upon you similar to the mountain of Sir"
"3564","Ali said:“I was ill and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by me while I was saying: ‘O Allah"
"3565","Ali narrated"
"3566","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say in his Witr: “O Allah"
"3567","Mus`ab bin Sa`d and `Amr bin Maimun narrated:“Sa`d used to teach his children these words just as the Muktib teaches children"
"3568","Aishah bint Sa`d bin Abi Waqqas narrated from her father"
"3569","Az-Zubair bin `Awwam narrated:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There is not a morning that the slave of Allah reached except that a caller calls out: ‘Glorify the King"
"3570","Ikrimah"
"3571","Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Ask Allah of His Bounty. For verily"
"3572","Zaid bin Arqam [may Allah be pleased with him] said that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say:“O Allah"
"3573","Jubair bin Nufair narrated that `Ubadah bin As-Samit narrated to them that"
"3574","Al-Bara’ bin `Azib narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“When you go to your bed"
"3575","Mu`adh bin `Abdullah bin Khubaib"
"3576","Abdullah bin Busr narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed with my father.” So he said: “We brought some food near him"
"3577","Bilal bin Yasar bin Zaid [the freed slave of the Prophet(ﷺ)] narrated:“My father narrated to me"
"3578","Uthman bin Hunaif narrated that a blind man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said:“Supplicate to Allah to heal me.” He (ﷺ) said: “If you wish I will supplicate for you"
"3579","Abu Umamah [may Allah be pleased with him] said:`Amr bin `Abasah reported to me that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “The closest that the Lord is to a worshipper is during the last part of the night"
"3580","Umarah bin Za`karah said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying; ‘Indeed"
"3581","Qais bin Sa`d bin `Ubadah narrated"
"3582","Safwan bin Sulaim said:“No angel has risen from the earth until he said: ‘There is no might or power except with Allah (Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh).’”"
"3583","Humaidah bint Yasir narrated from her grandmother Yusairah - and she was one of those who emigrated - she said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to us: ‘Hold fast to At-Tasbih"
"3584","Anas narrated that when the Prophet (ﷺ) would go out for an expedition"
"3585","Amr bin Shu`aib narrated from his father"
"3586","Umar bin Al-Khattab said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught me"
"3587","Asim bin Kulaib Al-Jarmi narrated from his father"
"3588","Muhammad bin Sulaim narrated:“Thabit Al-Bunani narrated to me"
"3589","Umm Salamah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught me"
"3590","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“No worshipper has ever said: None has the right to be worshipped but Allah (Lā ilāha illallāh)’ sincerely"
"3591","Ziyad bin `Ilaqah narrated from his uncle"
"3592","Ibn `Umar [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a man among the people said: ‘Allah is most exceedingly great"
"3593","Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited him"
"3594","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The supplication is not rejected between the Adhan and the Iqamah.” They said: “So what should we say"
"3595","Anas [bin Malik] narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“The supplication is not rejected between the Adhan and the Iqamah.”"
"3596","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The Mufarridun have preceded.” They said: “And who are the Mufarridun"
"3597","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“That I should say: ‘Glory is to Allah (Subḥān Allāh).’ ‘All praise is due to Allah (Al-ḥamdulillāh)"
"3598","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“There are three whose supplication is not rejected: The fasting person when he breaks his fast"
"3599","Abu Hurairah"
"3600","Abu Hurairah or Abu Sa`eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Indeed"
"3601","Abu Hurairah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: ‘Be frequent in saying: “There is no might or power except by Allah"
"3602","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Every Prophet has a (special) supplication which is answered. Verily"
"3603","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah"
"3604","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of Hell"
"3605","Narrated Wathilah bin Al-Asqa':that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah has chosen Isma'il from the children of Ibrahim"
"3606","Narrated Wathilah bin Al-Asqa':that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed"
"3607","Narrated Al-'Abbas bin 'Abdul-Muttalib:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed the Quraish have sat and spoken between themselves about the best of them"
"3608","Narrated Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada'ah:""Al-Abbas came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3609","Narrated Abu Hurairah:""They said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! When was the Prophethood established for you?' He said: 'While Adam was between (being) soul and body"
"3610","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the first of the people to appear upon their being resurrected"
"3611","Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the first for whom the earth will be split"
"3612","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Ask Allah to grant me Al-Wasilah."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And what is Al-Wasilah?"" He said: ""The highest level of Paradise. No one will attain it except for one man"
"3613","Narrated At-Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka'b:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The parable of me and the Prophets is that of a man who built a house"
"3614","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If you hear the Muadh-dhin then say as he says. Then send Salat upon me"
"3615","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Judgement"
"3616","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that a group of people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat waiting for him. He said: ""Then he came out"
"3617","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Salam:""The description of Muhammad is written in the Tawrah"
"3618","Narrated Anas bin Malik:""On the day in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Al-Madinah"
"3619","Narrated Al-Muttalib bin 'Abdullah bin Qais bin Makhramah:from his father"
"3620","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:""Abu Talib departed to Ash-Sham"
"3621","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) received Revelation when he was forty years old. So he stayed in Makkah for thirteen years and in Al-Madinah for ten. And he died when he was sixty-three years old"
"3622","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"
"3623","Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not very tall nor was he [very] short"
"3624","Narrated Simak bin Harb:from Jabir bin Samurah"
"3625","Narrated Abu Al-'Ala:from Samurah bin Jundab that he said: ""We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) and we would take turns (eating) from a bowl from the morning till the evening. Ten would stand and ten would sit."" We said: ""So what was filling it up?' He said: ""What are you amazed at? It wasn't filled up from anywhere but here"
"3626","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:""I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah. We departed to one of its suburbs"
"3627","Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to give Khutbah next to a tree"
"3628","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'How shall I know that you are a Prophet?' He said: 'If I were to call this date cluster from this palm tree"
"3629","Narrated Abu Zaid bin Akhtab:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wiped his hand over my face and supplicated for me."" 'Azrah (one of the narrators) said: ""Indeed he lived for one-hundred and twenty years"
"3630","Narrated Anas bin Malik:""Abu Talhah said to Umm Sulaim: 'I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sounding weak and I sensed some hunger in it. Do you have anything? She said: 'Yes.' So she got some loaves of wheat bread"
"3631","Narrated Anas bin Malik:""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the time when the 'Asr prayer had drawn near"
"3632","Narrated 'Aishah:""The first of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) initiated with of Prophethood"
"3633","Narrated 'Abdullah:""You consider the signs to be punishment"
"3634","Narrated 'Aishah:that Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the Prophet (ﷺ): 'How does the Revelation come to you?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell and that is the hardest upon me"
"3635","Narrated Al-Bara:""I have not seen anyone with hair past his shoulders in a red Hullah more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He had hair that would flow on his shoulders"
"3636","Narrated Abu Ishaq:""A man asked Al-Bara: 'Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like a sword?' He said: 'No"
"3637","Narrated 'Ali:""The Prophet (ﷺ) was not tall nor was he short"
"3638","Narrated Ibrahim bin Muhammad"
"3639","Narrated 'Urwah:that 'Aishah said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not speak quickly like you do now"
"3640","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would repeat a statement three times so that it could be understood"
"3641","Narrated Ibn Jaz:""I have not seen anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3642","Narrated Ibn Jaz:""The laughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not but smiling"
"3643","Narrated As-Sa'ib bin Yazid:""My maternal aunt took me to the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3644","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The seal of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"" - meaning the one which was between his two shoulder blades - ""was fleshy and red"
"3645","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The two shins of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were thin"
"3646","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a wide mouth (Dali' Al-Fam)"
"3647","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a wide mouth (Dali' Al-Fam)"
"3648","Narrated Abu Hurairah:""I have not seen anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the sun flowed upon his face. And I have not seen anyone quicker in his walking than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the earth was made easy for him. We would be exerting ourselves while he would not be struggling"
"3649","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The Prophets were presented to me"
"3650","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"
"3651","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"
"3652","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) stayed in Makkah for thirteen years - meaning while he was receiving Revelation - and he died when he was sixty-three years old"
"3653","Narrated Jabir [bin 'Abdullah]:that he heard Mu'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan giving a Khutbah"
"3654","Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-three years old"
"3655","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I free myself of the friendship of every Khalil"
"3656","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab:""Abu Bakr is our chief"
"3657","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Shaqiq:""I said to 'Aishah: 'Which of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) were the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' She said: 'Abu Bakr.' I said: 'Then who?' She said: ''Umar.' I said: ""Then who?' She said: 'Then Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.'"" He said: ""I said: 'Then who?''"" He said: ""Then she was silent"
"3658","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed the people of the higher levels"
"3659","Narrated Ibn Abi Mu'alla:from his father: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a Khutbah one day and said: 'Indeed there is a man whose Lord has given him the choice between living in this life as long as he wishes to live"
"3660","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat upon the Minbar and said: 'Indeed a worshiper has been given a choice by Allah"
"3661","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no favor due upon us from anyone"
"3662","Narrated Hudhaifah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Stick to the two after me"
"3663","Narrated Hudhaifah [may Allah be pleased with him]:""We were sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: 'I do not know how long I will be with you"
"3664","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about Abu Bakr and 'Umar: ""These two are the masters of the elder people among the inhabitants of Paradise. From the first ones and the last ones"
"3665","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:""I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3666","Narrated 'Ali:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Abu Bakr and 'Umar are the masters of the elder people among the inhabitants of Paradise"
"3667","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that Abu Bakr said: ""Am I not the most deserving of it among the people"
"3668","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go out to his Companions from The Muhajirin and the Ansar while they were sitting"
"3669","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) departed one day and entered the Masjid"
"3670","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Abu Bakr: ""You are my companion at the Hawd"
"3671","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Hantab:that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: ""These two are the hearing and the seeing"
"3672","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in Salat."" 'Aishah said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If Abu Bakr takes your place"
"3673","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""It is not befitting that a group"
"3674","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever spends a pair of things in the path of Allah"
"3675","Narrated Zaid bin Aslam:""I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'We were ordered by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to give in charity"
"3676","Narrated Jubair bin Mut'im:that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to speak to him about something. Then he ordered her with something"
"3677","Narrated Abu Salamah bin 'Abdur-Rahman:from Abu Hurairah"
"3678","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered the closing of all the gates"
"3679","Narrated 'Aishah:that Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3680","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no Prophet except that he has two ministers among the inhabitants of the heavens"
"3681","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah! Honor Islam through the most dear of these two men to you: Through Abu Jahl or through 'Umar bin Al-Khattab."" He said: ""And the most dear of them to Him was 'Umar"
"3682","Narrated Nafi':from Ibn 'Umar"
"3683","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah honor Islam through Abu Jahl bin Hisham or through 'Umar bin Al-Khattab."" He said: ""So it happened that 'Umar came the next day to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and accepted Islam"
"3684","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that 'Umar said to Abu Bakr: ""O best of people after the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)!"" So Abu Bakr said: ""If you say that"
"3685","Narrated Muhammad bin Sirin:""I don't think that a man who degrades Abu Bakr and 'Umar loves the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3686","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If there was to have a Prophet after me"
"3687","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I saw that I was brought a cup of milk"
"3688","Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""I entered Paradise and it was as if I was in a palace of gold. So I said: 'Whose palace is this?' They said: 'A youth's"
"3689","Narrated Abu Buraidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke in the morning and called for Bilal"
"3690","Narrated Buraidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out for one of his expeditions"
"3691","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting and we heard a scream and the voices of children. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arose"
"3692","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the first for whom the earth will split"
"3693","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Among the nations"
"3694","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you."" So Abu Bakr appeared. Then he said: ""A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you."" So 'Umar appeared"
"3695","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""While a man was tending some of his sheep"
"3696","Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was at Hira"
"3697","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"